          "body": "_This review was posted by an AI agent (OpenHands)._\n\nReviewed head `8189e214720e18de9236907b9c5d4cf8c2518392` against the current `main`, with a fresh read of the PR, its reviews/comments (none), and the linked issues #18505 and #18004 (both open, both carrying `ready-for-dev` and `priority:low`).\n\nScope: this is Canvas presentation in `src/components/features/chat/components/context-window-meter.tsx` plus its theme-contrast test. It owns the popover surface and tone maps, so it belongs in `OpenHands/OpenHands`; no server, wire-contract, or persisted-state surface is touched.\n\nWhat I verified on the head:\n- The tone maps now resolve from the same semantic roles the sibling Usage drawer (`usage-panel/context-meter.tsx`) already uses: `text-feedback-warning`/`text-feedback-error` for labels and `bg-feedback-warning`/`bg-status-error` for fills. No new palette token is added; per-theme overrides (Light+, Solarized Light, DeepSea) are inherited.\n- The popover is now `bg-surface-raised`, which matches the surface the contrast test already measured (`--oh-surface-raised`), so the test and the rendered backdrop are consistent instead of measuring a surface the component did not use.\n- The bar keeps its 6px height (`h-1.5`); the 1px `border` with `borderColor: CONTEXT_WINDOW_TRACK_COLOR` adds the full-range boundary without growing the bar, and the absolutely-positioned fill (`inset-y-0 left-0`) sits inside the padding box, so the boundary stays visible under the fill.\n- The diff only extends the existing five-theme checks (adds `--oh-foreground` to the fill-vs-track loop and a composited boundary check); no assertion is removed or weakened.\n\nEvidence and CI: authenticated local Agent Server 1.55.1 + real `deepseek/deepseek-flash` before/after GIF, MP4, and a five-theme PNG are linked and are appropriate for a static-render color change; the latest `Validate PR description`, `CI / test-and-build (ubuntu)`, and `test-and-build (windows)` check runs on this head are green. The `release ready` `startup_failure` is not head-specific: every recent run of that reusable workflow fails at startup across unrelated branches.\n\nFocused tests in the workspace: `__tests__/themes/color-themes.test.tsx`, `context-window-ring.test.tsx`, `context-window-meter.test.tsx`, and `usage-panel/context-meter.test.tsx` plus the surrounding chat/usage/theme suites: 118 passed, 38 of them the directly-scoped color/ring/meter files.\n\nAcceptance criteria checklist (issue #18505):\n- [x] Warning/danger labels meet 4.5:1 on the popover surface in all five themes (asserted against `--oh-surface-raised`).\n- [x] Neutral, warning, and danger fills meet 3:1 against the track; the full-range boundary meets 3:1 against the popover surface (composited check).\n- [x] Tones resolve from semantic feedback roles; no shared palette token added or modified.\n- [x] Thresholds (70%/90%), ring, compaction, and Usage navigation unchanged; existing handlers and tests still pass.\n- [x] `npm run lint` / `npm run build` gates are green on this head in CI.\n- [x] Theme contract in `__tests__/themes/color-themes.test.tsx` covers the popover surface and its boundary.\n\nNon-blocking, already disclosed by the author: the change moves the popover backdrop from `--oh-color-tertiary` to `--oh-surface-raised`, which slightly improves (but does not fix) the unrelated muted-text contrast in Solarized Light; issue #18505 scopes muted text and the ring's fixed amber/red arc out of this change, so this is not a merge gate.\n\nNo material correctness, security, compatibility, architecture, or evidence gaps found.\n\n\u2705 APPROVED",
